 "questions": [
  {
   "id": 668855,
   "is_answer_order_important": false,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "<ol start=\"8\">\n<li>A kindergarten teacher bought $21 worth of stickers and cardstock for his class. The stickers cost $1.50 a sheet and the cardstock cost $3.50 per pack. The equation <span data-math=\"1.5s + 3.5c =21\">1.5s + 3.5c =21</span> represents the relationship between sheets of stickers, <span data-math=\"s\">s</span>, packs of cardstocks, <span data-math=\"c\">c</span>, and the dollar amount a kindergarten teacher spent on these supplies.<br><br>What does the vertical intercept, (0,6), mean in this situation?</li>\n</ol><img alt=\"Line on grid, origin O. Horizontal axis, 0 to 18 by 2’s, sheets of stickers. Vertical axis, 0 to 10 by 2’s, packs of cardstock. Line passes through points 0 comma 6, 7 comma 3, and 14 comma 0.\" height=\"140\" src=\"exercises/media/c2bd267ac4b2ba11.svg\" title=\"kehVi8A4H5nQTNwBQqGvLNa9\" width=\"239\">",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1333567,
     "content_html": "14 sheets of stickers and 6 packs of cardstock were bought."
    },
    {
     "id": 1333568,
     "content_html": "7 sheets of stickers and 3 packs of cardstock were bought."
    },
    {
     "id": 1333569,
     "content_html": "6 sheets of stickers and 0 packs of cardstock were bought."
    },
    {
     "id": 1333570,
     "content_html": "0 sheets of stickers and 6 packs of cardstock were bought."
    }
   ],
